  "_comment": "One tree per combat style, and a character has one: their path's -- the hero the blade, the warden the bow, the wayfarer the staff. A tree earns a point at every third level of its skill. A node needs its milestone level in that skill and at least one rank of the node above it in its branch; each rank costs a point, and 'effects' is what one rank gives (fractions unless noted: damage 0.04 is +4%). Eight rows, at 5, 15, 30, 40, 47, 54, 62 and 70 -- closer together as levels come slower: two passives of three ranks, a technique (a move that replaces the charged heavy attack once chosen), an ability (a move of its own with a cooldown and a cost, carried in one of three slots: guard + light, guard + heavy, guard + lock on), a passive of two ranks that asks when, a second ability, a second passive of two, and a capstone. Forty-two ranks a tree against thirty-three points by level 99. The melee tree has a fourth branch, Footwork, for moves made on the run; it is not a full column and its nodes need nothing above them.",
